  "complete_algorithm_gate": false,
  "scope": "Native object primitives: distinct resident Entry addresses derive cardinality bounds; disjoint occupied Arc<Node> payload and Box<Branch> regions survive allocation, same-shape writes, branch-to-leaf conversion and justified reclamation. Explicit per-child retained Arc tokens support arbitrary snapshot-release interleavings during COW. Successful payload allocation moves those tokens into edges; assignment and interleaved old-token teardown preserve the copied value, unique fresh root, saved roots and object-region invariants. The no-Weak Arc behavior is an explicit pinned library/compiler contract. This does not establish all Rust/native layouts, buffers, mutation places, physical word loops or full algorithm extraction.",
  "remaining": [
    "Compose pinned Arc contracts with root and mutable edge slots in all concrete mutation paths; cover external snapshot cloning as well as the proved release-only environment and connect private source representation to token ownership",
    "Native byte/edge/frame buffers and in-flight payload/Box moves, allocation/layout correspondence and successful-operation limits",
    "Derive routing/query buffer bounds and compose concrete graph loops and size updates with native word arithmetic, preserving late leaf scope release",
    "Exact-source Rust/model differential histories and meaningful faults before predeclared original/long/injective-varied-prefix throughput/mean/p99 and allocation comparisons",
    "Runtime promotion still requires matched benefit, local correctness, ordinary recovery, actual Chaos Mesh and three-copy Redis throughput/latency"
  ]
}
